window.PRACTICE_SET={"number":6,"sections":[{"name":"Verbal Reasoning · Section 1","minutes":18,"questions":[{"type":"multi","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Each of the country's 26 sates and most of its more than 2,000 municipalities have their own police forces, <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> communication and making it difficult to establish a coordinated law-enforcement strategy.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"establishing"},{"key":"B","text":"impeding"},{"key":"C","text":"hampering"},{"key":"D","text":"launching"},{"key":"E","text":"obscuring"},{"key":"F","text":"preventing"}],"answer":["B","C"],"id":"sentence-equivalence-e9c04051d059","source":"KMF · Sentence Equivalence","translation":"국가의 26개 국가와 2,000개 이상의 지방 자치 단체의 대부분은 자체 경찰력을 보유하고 있어 의사 소통을 방해하고 조정된 법 집행 전략을 수립하기 어렵습니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Our study revealed that nest-guarding long-tailed skinks (a species of lizard) homed (returned to their nests) more successfully when displaced shorter distances. There are two reasons why homing success rates decreased with increasing displacement distance. One possibility is that females were simply displaced too far to find their way home. However, this is unlikely given that some individuals managed to find their way home from each distance we used. The second possibility deals with trade-offs between the risks associated with making a long return trip and the benefits of returning. Animals should expend energy only when the associated costs are low. As reptiles increase the time spent moving, their daily energy expenditure increases dramatically. The energetic costs of returning home and the chances that the eggs will have been preyed upon during the return trip both increase substantially as displacement distance increases. For example, the 130 hours (5.5 days) that female skinks spent returning from a distance of 300 meters is sufficient for an egg- eating snake to locate and prey upon the entire clutch. However, females with larger clutches were more likely to home at distances over 50 meters. For these females, the relative fitness benefits associated with having more eggs successfully hatch may outweigh the energetic costs of returning to a nest site, even if the nest may have already been preyed upon."],"prompt":"The claim in the highlighted sentence assumes which of the following about the individuals that managed to find their way home from each distance?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"They were less able to detect egg-eating predators than were the other long-tailed skinks studied."},{"key":"B","text":"They were more averse to risk than were the other long- tailed skinks studied"},{"key":"C","text":"They expended less energy when homing than did the other long-tailed skinks studied."},{"key":"D","text":"They did not possess better homing skills than did the other long-tailed skinks studied."},{"key":"E","text":"They had significantly smaller clutches than did the other long-tailed skinks studied."}],"answer":["D"],"id":"long-reading-fb7b9665a8bd","source":"KMF · Long Reading","translation":"강조 표시된 문장의 주장은 각 거리에서 집으로 가는 길을 찾았던 개인에 대해 다음 중 어느 것을 가정합니까? 그들은 알을 먹는 포식자를 덜 감지했습니다","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">One <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> is that so far, Web services have turned out to be much harder to deliver than their champions had hoped.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"hope"},{"key":"B","text":"snag"},{"key":"C","text":"prospect"},{"key":"D","text":"hitch"},{"key":"E","text":"upshot"},{"key":"F","text":"reason"}],"answer":["B","D"],"id":"sentence-equivalence-c493d1982106","source":"KMF · Sentence Equivalence","translation":"한 가지 문제는 지금까지 웹 서비스가 챔피언이 기대했던 것보다 훨씬 더 어려운 것으로 판명되었다는 것입니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Although the passenger pigeons, now extinct, were abundant in eighteenth- and nineteenth-century America, archaeological studies at twelfth-century Cahokian sites in the present day United States examined household food trash and found that traces of passenger pigeon were quite rare. Given that the sites were close to a huge passenger pigeon roost documented by John James Audubon in the nineteenth century and that Cahokians consumed almost every other animal protein source available, the archaeologists conducting the studies concluded the passenger pigeon population had once been very limited before increasing dramatically in post-columbian America. Other archaeologists have criticized those conclusions on the grounds that passenger pigeon bones would not be likely to be preserved. But all the archaeological projects found plenty of bird bones- and even tiny bones from fish."],"prompt":"Which of the following, if true, would most call into question the reasoning of \"the archaeologists conducting the studiesll?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Audubon was unable to correctly identify twelfth- century Cahokian sites"},{"key":"B","text":"Audubon made his observations before passenger pigeon populations began to decline."},{"key":"C","text":"Passenger pigeons would have been attracted to household food trash"},{"key":"D","text":"Archaeologist have found passenger pigeon remains among food waste at eighteenth-century human settlements"},{"key":"E","text":"Passenger pigeons tended not to roost at the same sites for very many generations"}],"answer":["E"],"id":"short-reading-84827118f31f","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"다음 중 사실이라면 \"연구를 수행하는 고고학자들이?","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"blank","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Astronomers have always suspected that planets might orbit stars other than our sun but <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  that they would find systems structured much like our own solar system. Yet a flood of recent discoveries has made it clear that extrasolar planetary systems can <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  our own solar system.</p>","groups":[[{"key":"A","text":"imagined"},{"key":"B","text":"verified"},{"key":"C","text":"doubted"}],[{"key":"D","text":"be affected by"},{"key":"E","text":"differ dramatically from"},{"key":"F","text":"reveal characteristics about"}]],"answer":["A","E"],"id":"double-blank-c9c112a17030","source":"KMF · Double-blank Text Completion","translation":"천문학자들은 항상 행성이 우리 태양 이외의 별을 공전할 수 있다고 의심했지만 (i) 그들이 우리 자신의 태양계와 매우 유사한 구조를 가진 시스템을 찾을 것이라고 상상했습니다. 그러나 최근 발견의 홍수는 외계 행성계가 (ii) 우리 자신의 태양계와 극적으로 다를 수 있음을 분명히 했습니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Although most of the lakes have merged, salinity levels are not <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> throughout the lake systems: an upward-trending salinity gradient extends southeast from Pelican Lake to East Stump Lake, a distance of nearly 80 kilometers.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"known"},{"key":"B","text":"equable"},{"key":"C","text":"rising"},{"key":"D","text":"problematic"},{"key":"E","text":"unprecedented"}],"answer":["B"],"id":"single-blank-df735776224e","source":"KMF · Single-blank Text Completion","translation":"대부분의 호수가 합쳐졌지만 염분 수준은 호수 시스템 전체에서 동일하지 않습니다. 상향 경향의 염분 기울기는 Pelican Lake에서 East Stump Lake까지 남동쪽으로 뻗어 있으며 거의 80km의 거리입니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Whereas Carlos Bulosan aimed through fiction and personal testimony to advance both Filipino civil rights in the United States and the social transformation of the Philippines, Yen Le Espiritu has set herself the task of recovering life histories of Filipino Americans. Her work brings Filipino Americans of the generation following the 1934-1965 immigration hiatus graphically to life. A special strength is the representation of Filipino American women, who were scarce among immigrants before the 1934 American curb on Filipino immigration but composed more than half of the immigrants to America since liberalization in 1965. Espiritu's subjects document their changing sense of Filipino identity in the United States, much as Bulosan did as a member of the first substantial wave of immigrants."],"prompt":"According to the passage, both Bulosan and Espiritu do which of the following in their work?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Consider generational differences in Filipino immigrants, responses to life in the United States"},{"key":"B","text":"Attempt to make allowance for the demographic variations among Filipino immigrants to the United States"},{"key":"C","text":"Employ fiction in addition to documenting actual life histories of Filipino immigrants to the United States"},{"key":"D","text":"Represent how life in the United States has affected immigrants, sense of Filipino identity"},{"key":"E","text":"Examine the effects on Filipinos in the United States of the 1934 American curb on Filipino immigration"}],"answer":["D"],"id":"short-reading-8d42399d1d87","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"이 구절에 따르면 불로산과 에스피리투는 다음 중 어느 것을 합니까? 필리핀의 세대 차이를 고려하십시오","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Scientist reported last month on a sign of relative solar <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> the solar wind, a rush of charged particles continually spewed from the Sun at a million miles an hour, had diminished to its lowest level in 50 years.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"quiescence"},{"key":"B","text":"turbulence"},{"key":"C","text":"isolation"},{"key":"D","text":"calm"},{"key":"E","text":"remoteness"},{"key":"F","text":"instability"}],"answer":["A","D"],"id":"sentence-equivalence-a3dd7b28a85a","source":"KMF · Sentence Equivalence","translation":"과학자들은 지난달 상대적으로 태양열을 고요하게 만들었다고 보고했다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Scientific consensus is that humans first began to have a warming effect on Earth's climate within the past century, after coal- burning factories, power plants, and motor vehicles began releasing carbon dioxide (CO2) and other greenhouse gases in significant quantities into the air. However, evidence suggests that human agricultural activities may have had such an effect much earlier:concentrations of CO2 started rising about 8000 years ago, even though natural trends indicate they should have been dropping; methane levels rose similarly about 3,000 years later. Without these rises, however, current temperatures in northern parts of North America and Europe would be cooler by three to four degrees Celsius-enough to inhibit agriculture-and an ice age would probably have begun several thousand years ago in northeastern Canada."],"prompt":"Which of the following best describes the function of the highlighted sentence?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"It undermines the assumption that human activity has had a significant impact on Earth's climate"},{"key":"B","text":"It supports the assumption that Earth's temperatures have risen appreciably over the past 100 years"},{"key":"C","text":"It questions the assumption that greenhouse gases have had a warming effect on Earth's climate"},{"key":"D","text":"It challenges the assumption that human activity began to affect Earth's climate after the advent of industrialization"},{"key":"E","text":"It supports the assumption that greenhouse gases are a direct by-product of industrial activities"}],"answer":["D"],"id":"short-reading-e7e821be0050","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"다음 중 강조 표시된 문장의 기능을 가장 잘 설명한 것은? 그것은 인간의 활동이","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Growing grapes in greenhouses containing air enriched with carbon dioxide increases crop yields, an effect that is enhanced when the growing temperature is also raised several degrees. Although enclosed cultivation is impractical in vineyards, increases in yields from grape cultivation in the open can be expected because emissions from the burning of fossil fuels will almost certainly lead to an increase in the carbon dioxide content of atmospheric air over the next century."],"prompt":"Which of the following, if true, most weakens the argument?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"When grapes are grown in greenhouses, it is relatively easy to control the grape pests that thrive in air enriched with carbon dioxide."},{"key":"B","text":"Recent improvements in pest control have increased grape yields in many vineyards."},{"key":"C","text":"Increasing carbon dioxide levels in greenhouses has not been shown to improve the quality of grapes grown in greenhouses."},{"key":"D","text":"Increasing carbon dioxide levels in greenhouses increases the sweetness of raisins made from grapes grown in the greenhouses."},{"key":"E","text":"As the carbon dioxide level in the open air increases, temperatures at the Earth's surface will also increase."}],"answer":["A"],"id":"logic-4d9fc231fad0","source":"KMF · Logical Reasoning","translation":"","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Because people expect theater directors to be authoritarians, many were surprised that Clark was so<span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"histrionic"},{"key":"B","text":"megalomaniacal"},{"key":"C","text":"egalitarian"},{"key":"D","text":"indolent"},{"key":"E","text":"charismatic"}],"answer":["C"],"id":"single-blank-8685aa4e59fb","source":"KMF · Single-blank Text Completion","translation":"사람들은 연극 감독이 권위주의적인 사람이 되기를 기대하기 때문에 클락이 그렇게 평등하다는 사실에 많은 사람들이 놀랐습니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">The stories in Yiyun Li's recent collection are distinctive particularly for the strong contrast between their emotional intensity and their consistently <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> tone.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"affable"},{"key":"B","text":"ebullient"},{"key":"C","text":"measured"},{"key":"D","text":"irascible"},{"key":"E","text":"overwrought"}],"answer":["C"],"id":"single-blank-e5ad0fea1b87","source":"KMF · Single-blank Text Completion","translation":"리이윤의 최근 컬렉션에 실린 이야기는 감정의 강도와 일관되게 측정된 음색의 강한 대조로 특히 독특합니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."}]},{"name":"Verbal Reasoning · Section 2","minutes":23,"questions":[{"type":"multi","passage":["Soil communities are dependent on plants for organic matter. Plants provide organic matter for soil communities through the decomposition of leaf litter, by oozing nutrients from roots, or through other methods of deposition of organic compounds into the soil environments. As a result of these diverse methods by which plants supply resources, unique soil communities fomi under different plant species and under plant communities that differ in composition. If a nonnative plant species invades an above-ground community of flora and fauna, it can alter links between the native above-ground community and the below- ground soil community. For example, an invading nonnative plant could alter the quantity of leaf litter production, which would alter nutrient contributions to the soil."],"prompt":"Consider each of the choices separately and select all that apply. Which of the following statements about the connection between above-ground plants and below-ground soil communities can be inferred from the passage?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Because of the nature of the link between above-and below-ground communities, many soil communities are deficient in nutrients."},{"key":"B","text":"The extent to which soil communities are dependent on above-ground plants is extremely variable from one soil community to another."},{"key":"C","text":"Because different plants supply resources to soil communities in different ways, distinctive soil communities form under different plant communities."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"short-reading-143744cef3ef","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"각 선택 사항을 별도로 고려하고 적용되는 모든 항목을 선택하십시오. 지상 식물과 지하 토양 군집 사이의 연관성에 대한 다음 설명 중 통로에서 추론할 수 있는 것은 무엇입니까? 위와 의 연결 특성 때문입니다","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"blank","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Although movie critic Pauline Kael had a distaste for sycophancy, she also had a need for <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  as a consequence of these competing feelings, she sent very <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  signals to friends and colleagues.</p>","groups":[[{"key":"A","text":"solitude"},{"key":"B","text":"obeisance"},{"key":"C","text":"clarity"}],[{"key":"D","text":"direct"},{"key":"E","text":"subtle"},{"key":"F","text":"mixed"}]],"answer":["B","F"],"id":"double-blank-790c3881f02d","source":"KMF · Double-blank Text Completion","translation":"영화 평론가인 Pauline Kael은 아첨을 싫어했지만 (i) 이러한 경쟁적인 감정의 결과로 경의가 필요했지만 그녀는 친구와 동료에게 매우 (ii) 혼합 신호를 보냈습니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">One baffling aspect of the novel is its capacity to generate emotional power from a plot that lacks the most elementary <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> readers must accept not an occasional coincidence, but a continuous stream of them.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"synergy"},{"key":"B","text":"continuity"},{"key":"C","text":"naivety"},{"key":"D","text":"premise"},{"key":"E","text":"credibility"}],"answer":["E"],"id":"single-blank-9dc839ab452b","source":"KMF · Single-blank Text Completion","translation":"소설의 당혹스러운 측면 중 하나는 가장 기본적인 신뢰성이 결여된 플롯에서 감정적 힘을 생성하는 능력입니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Migratory songbirds breeding in Eurasia's temperate forests depend on a summer flush of insects, particularly caterpillars, to feed themselves and their offspring. In some places, these caterpillars are emerging earlier in responses to rising global temperatures. In theory9 the songbirds could simply push up their departure from their winter quarters to catch the earlier flush of insect prey. If, however, the birds rely on a fixed cue such as increasing day length to begin flying north, they may be unable to adjust the timing of their migration. Precisely this disruption in the emergence of insects relative to the timing of songbird migration has been identified as the cause of a significant decline in populations of pied flycatchers in the Netherlands."],"prompt":"According to the passage, populations of insects preyed upon by pied flycatchers.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"are finding less food as temperatures rise in the Eurasian forests that they inhabit"},{"key":"B","text":"are endangered because of global warming"},{"key":"C","text":"have recently experienced changes in the timing of their life cycles relative to the calendar"},{"key":"D","text":"have recently begun inhabiting cooler climates largely unfrequented by pied flycatchers."},{"key":"E","text":"have increased significantly because of lack of predation."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"short-reading-d66f7447a642","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"이 구절에 따르면 곤충의 개체군은 얼룩덜룩한 파리 캐쳐가 잡아먹는다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Among many historians a belief persists that Cotton Mather's biographies of some of the settlers of the Massachusetts Bay Colony (published 1702) are exercises in hagiography, endowing their subj ects with saintly piety at the expense of historical accuracy. Yet modern studies have profited both from the breadth of information that Mather provides in, for example, his discussions of colonial medicine and from his critical observations of such leading figures as Governor John Winthrop. Mather's wry humor as demonstrated by his detailed descriptions of events such as Winthrop's efforts to prevent wood-stealing is overlooked by those charging Mather with presenting his subjects as extremely pious. The charge also obscures Mather's concern with the settlers, material, not just spiritual, prosperity. Further, this pejorative view underrates the biographies, value as chronicles: Mather amassed all sorts of published and unpublished documents as sources, and his selection of key events shows a marked sensitivity to the nature of the colony's development."],"prompt":"Information in the passage best supports which of the following statements about Mather's biographies of the settlers of the Massachusetts Bay Colony.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Annals written by Mather and others were censored by later historians, thus detracting from their value as full and accurate accounts of the period."},{"key":"B","text":"Mather's description of Governor Winthrop includes all of Winthrop's shortcomings, such as a tendency toward levity at inappropriate times."},{"key":"C","text":"Mather's descriptions of the Massachusetts Bay colonists were based primarily on firsthand experiences."},{"key":"D","text":"Many historians believe that Mather's biographies are poor sources of historical information because biography is an inherently unreliable genre of historical writing."},{"key":"E","text":"Mather's writings reflect an interest in the degree of economic success achieved by early Massachusetts Bay colonists."}],"answer":["E"],"id":"long-reading-914bac27b7f6","source":"KMF · Long Reading","translation":"매사추세츠 만 식민지 정착민의 Mather의 전기에 대한 다음 설명 중 어느 것을 가장 잘 뒷받침하는 구절의 정보입니다. Mather와 다른 사람들이 작성한 연대기는 에 의해 검열되었습니다","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"blank","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Given children's active fantasy lives, one might think of truthfulness as <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  virtue in young children, but it turns out that lying is the more <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  skill. A child who is going to lie must recognize the truth, intellectually conceive of an alternate reality, and be able to convincingly sell that new reality to someone else. Therefore, lying <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span>  cognitive development and social skills in a way that honesty simply does not.</p>","groups":[[{"key":"A","text":"an instinctive"},{"key":"B","text":"an acquired"},{"key":"C","text":"a conscious"}],[{"key":"D","text":"advanced"},{"key":"E","text":"practical"},{"key":"F","text":"mundane"}],[{"key":"G","text":"undermines"},{"key":"H","text":"forgoes"},{"key":"I","text":"demands"}]],"answer":["B","D","I"],"id":"triple-blank-cd989b6578c3","source":"KMF · Triple-blank Text Completion","translation":"아이들의 활동적인 환상적 삶을 감안할 때 진실성은 (i) 어린 아이들의 후천적인 미덕으로 생각할 수 있지만 거짓말은 더 (ii) 고급 기술입니다. 거짓말을 하는 아이는 진리를 인식하고 지적으로 대체 현실을 생각해야 하며, 그 새로운 현실을 다른 사람에게 설득력 있게 판매할 수 있어야 합니다. 따라서 거짓말(iii)은 정직이 하지 않는 방식으로 인지 발달과 사회적 기술을 요구합니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Although vastly popular during its time, much nineteenth-century women's fiction in the United States went unread by the twentieth-century educated elite, who were taught to ignore it as didactic. However, American literature has a tradition of didacticism going back to its Puritan roots, shifting over time from sermons and poetic transcripts into novels, which proved to be perfect vehicles for conveying social values. In the nineteenth century, critics reviled Poe for neglecting to conclude his stories with pithy moral tags, while Longfellow was canonized for his didactic verse. Although rhetorical changes favoring the anti- didactic can be detected as nineteenth-century American transformed itself into a secular society, it was twentieth-century criticism, which placed aesthetic value above everything else, that had no place in its doctrine for the didacticism of others."],"prompt":"In the context in which it appears, \"conveying\" most nearly means","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"carrying"},{"key":"B","text":"transferring"},{"key":"C","text":"granting"},{"key":"D","text":"imparting"},{"key":"E","text":"projecting"}],"answer":["D"],"id":"short-reading-ab44f896681a","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"그것이 나타나는 맥락에서, \"전달\"은 거의 의미합니다","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["The use of nets at beach resorts to protect swimming areas from sharks has been criticized by environmentalists because the nets needlessly kill thousands of marine animals annually. However, environmentalists have recently discovered that an electrified cable buried beneath the periphery of swimming areas causes sharks to swim away while harming neither humans nor marine life. Hence, by installing such cables, resort communities will be able to maintain tourism while satisfying environmentalists, concerns."],"prompt":"Which of the following, if true, most seriously weakens the argument?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Many seaside resort communities where sharks have never been sighted nonetheless paid to install buried electrified cables."},{"key":"B","text":"Tourism at resorts where sharks have been sighted has suffered only slightly despite the fact that many people claim to fear sharks."},{"key":"C","text":"Because they have a strong fear of sharks, many tourists prefer to swim at beaches that are known to be well protected from sharks."},{"key":"D","text":"The buried electrified cable is not the only innovation approved by environmentalists that is l(nown to be successful in repelling sharks without hanning them"},{"key":"E","text":"The marine mammals that are a major tourist attraction at many resorts do not enter areas around which there are buried electrified cables."}],"answer":["E"],"id":"logic-52b49984b344","source":"KMF · Logical Reasoning","translation":"","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Any antimatter in our part of the universe is necessarily <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> because of the overwhelming preponderance of ordinary matter, by which antimatter is quickly annihilated.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"short-lived"},{"key":"B","text":"nebulous"},{"key":"C","text":"scarce"},{"key":"D","text":"concrete"},{"key":"E","text":"substantial"},{"key":"F","text":"ephemeral"}],"answer":["A","F"],"id":"sentence-equivalence-d2b2c5433788","source":"KMF · Sentence Equivalence","translation":"우리 우주의 모든 반물질은 반물질이 빠르게 소멸되는 일반적인 물질의 압도적인 우세 때문에 필연적으로 일시적입니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">The economist argued that however much the government might trumpet the value of <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> it had been as bold as any other in its spending programs.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"thrift"},{"key":"B","text":"consumption"},{"key":"C","text":"dialogue"},{"key":"D","text":"cooperation"},{"key":"E","text":"transparency"}],"answer":["A"],"id":"single-blank-1a1aa3ef6a6b","source":"KMF · Single-blank Text Completion","translation":"이코노미스트는 정부가 절약의 가치를 얼마나 많이 내세울 수 있더라도 지출 프로그램에서 다른 어떤 것보다 대담하다고 주장했습니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["Biologists studying wild monkeys sometimes need the genetic material DNA from a particular monkey to determine the animal's parentage. Until recently, DNA could be extracted only from blood. Collecting a blood sample required tranquilizing the donor animal. Now DNA can be extracted from hair. Monkeys shed large quantities of hair in places where they sleep. Therefore, researchers will now be able to determine the parentage of individual monkeys from DNA without tranquilizing the monkeys."],"prompt":"Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument depends?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"The places in which monkeys sleep are easily accessible to researchers."},{"key":"B","text":"Information about a particular monkey's parentage is the only kind of information that can be determined from DNA that has been extracted from that monkey's hair."},{"key":"C","text":"For at least some samples of hair collected from monkey habitat it will be possible to associate hairs with the individual monkeys from which they came."},{"key":"D","text":"Examining DNA is the only way to detemiine the parentage of wild monkeys."},{"key":"E","text":"It will be necessary to obtain any hair samples used in determining a monkey's parentage from a place where the monkey has slept."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"logic-5fe3dddd4bb2","source":"KMF · Logical Reasoning","translation":"","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["In mountainous regions, the timberline is the highest altitude at which trees grow. In the Rocky Mountains, the current timberline is at the altitude above which growing season temperatures remain cooler than 10 degrees centigrade. Fossilized remains of trees that grew l 0,000 years ago have been found l 00 meters above the current Rocky Mountain timberline. Clearly, therefore, the climate of the Rocky Mountains is cooler now than it was l 0,000 years ago."],"prompt":"Which of the following is an assumption on which the argument relies?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"In the past l 0,000 years, the only trees to have grown above today's timberline are the trees whose fossilized remains been found."},{"key":"B","text":"No trees grew l 0,000 years ago at altitudes higher than the ones at which fossilized tree remains have been found."},{"key":"C","text":"The fossils are not of species of trees that were able to tolerate cooler growing temperatures than are the species that currently grow near the timberline."},{"key":"D","text":"The Rocky Mountains have not eroded significantly over the past 10,000 years."},{"key":"E","text":"The climate of the Rocky Mountains has never been significantly warmer than during the lifetime of the trees whose fossilized remains have been found."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"logic-1ce5255a723c","source":"KMF · Logical Reasoning","translation":"","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">The professor's habitual air of <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> was misleading front, concealing amazing reserves of patience and a deep commitment to his students, learning.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"cordiality"},{"key":"B","text":"irascibility"},{"key":"C","text":"disorganization"},{"key":"D","text":"conviviality"},{"key":"E","text":"diffidence"},{"key":"F","text":"exasperation"}],"answer":["B","F"],"id":"sentence-equivalence-29971a8fc161","source":"KMF · Sentence Equivalence","translation":"그 교수의 습관적인 분노는 오해의 소지가 있는 전면이었고, 놀라운 인내심과 그의 학생들에 대한 깊은 헌신, 학습에 대한 깊은 헌신을 숨겼습니다.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"<p class=\"question-stem\">Individuals interested in longevity have sought to fine-tune their bodies with all kinds of <span class=\"blank-token\" aria-label=\"blank\"></span> diets: only raw foods; only plant; only the flesh, fruit, and nuts that prehistoric humans would have hunted and foraged.</p>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"eccentric"},{"key":"B","text":"meager"},{"key":"C","text":"salutary"},{"key":"D","text":"proscriptive"},{"key":"E","text":"trendy"},{"key":"F","text":"exacting"}],"answer":["D","F"],"id":"sentence-equivalence-26f93668a476","source":"KMF · Sentence Equivalence","translation":"장수에 관심이 있는 개인은 모든 종류의 엄격한 식단으로 몸을 미세 조정하려고 노력했습니다. 생식만; 유일한 식물; 선사 시대 인간이 사냥하고 먹이를 먹었던 살과 열매와 견과만.","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."},{"type":"single","passage":["In general, naive individuals appear more likely to learn from interaction with familiar rather than unfamiliar members of their species. Kaveliers and colleagues (2005) reported that naive laboratory-bred deer mice showed greater social learning of defensive responses to biting flies after observing responses of familiar members than after observing responses of unfamiliar members. Earlier, Valsecchi and colleagues (1996) reported striking differences in social learning of food preferences among Mongolian gerbils, depending on whether they were exposed to familiar or unfamiliar demonstrators. At the time, this was unexpected because Gaief and colleagues (1984)had previously reported no familiarity effect in Norway rats on social learning of food preferences. However, Gaief et al (1998) subsequently uncovered a significant familiarity effect that was evident when demonstrators are some hours before interacting with observers but absent when demonstrators are immediately before interacting."],"prompt":"Which of the following can be inferred about the report by Gaief and colleagues (1984) as it is described in the passage?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"It introduced a concept that the report by Kaveliers and colleagues was intended to clarify."},{"key":"B","text":"It highlighted an inaccuracy in the report by Valsecchi and colleagues"},{"key":"C","text":"It led to an incorrect supposition on the part of some scientists"},{"key":"D","text":"It played an important role in developing an understanding of social learning between members of different species."},{"key":"E","text":"It suggested that the familiarity effect is stronger in some species than in others."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"short-reading-b8d07f58e8e0","source":"KMF · Short Reading","translation":"다음 중 Gaief와 동료들(1984)이 이 구절에 설명된 보고서에 대해 추론할 수 있는 것은 무엇입니까? 그것은 Kaveliers의 보고서와","vocabulary":[],"explanation":"정답 선지를 문맥에 넣어 문장의 논리와 의미가 자연스럽게 이어지는지 확인하세요."}]},{"name":"Quantitative Reasoning · Section 1","minutes":21,"questions":[{"type":"multi","prompt":"In a certain sequence of numbers, each term after the first term is found by multiplying the preceding term by 2 and then subtracting 3 from the product. If the 4th term in the sequence is 19, which of the following numbers are in the sequence?<br><br>Indicate <u>all</u> such numbers.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"8"},{"key":"C","text":"11"},{"key":"D","text":"16"},{"key":"E","text":"22"},{"key":"F","text":"35"}],"answer":["A","C","F"],"id":"quant-4-13","source":"Quant Practice Set 4 · Q13","explanation":"정답은 A. 5, C. 11, F. 35입니다."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"coordinate-plane\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 520 260\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Coordinate plane with point A at 1 comma 0 and point B at 6 comma 0.\">\n      <defs>\n        <marker id=\"arrow\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"5\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L0,6 L6,3 z\" fill=\"#20262c\"/></marker>\n      </defs>\n      <line x1=\"55\" y1=\"205\" x2=\"470\" y2=\"205\" stroke=\"#20262c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n      <line x1=\"85\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"85\" y2=\"22\" stroke=\"#20262c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"/>\n      <g stroke=\"#20262c\" stroke-width=\"2\" font-family=\"Arial\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n        <line x1=\"140\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"212\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"232\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">1</text>\n        <line x1=\"195\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"195\" y2=\"212\"/><text x=\"195\" y=\"232\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">2</text>\n        <line x1=\"250\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"212\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"232\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">3</text>\n        <line x1=\"305\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"305\" y2=\"212\"/><text x=\"305\" y=\"232\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">4</text>\n        <line x1=\"360\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"212\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"232\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">5</text>\n        <line x1=\"415\" y1=\"198\" x2=\"415\" y2=\"212\"/><text x=\"415\" y=\"232\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">6</text>\n        <line x1=\"78\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"170\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"176\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">1</text>\n        <line x1=\"78\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"135\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"141\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">2</text>\n        <line x1=\"78\" y1=\"100\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"100\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"106\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">3</text>\n        <line x1=\"78\" y1=\"65\" x2=\"92\" y2=\"65\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"71\" stroke=\"none\" fill=\"#20262c\">4</text>\n      </g>\n      <circle cx=\"140\" cy=\"205\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#20262c\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"189\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-size=\"22\" font-style=\"italic\">A</text>\n      <circle cx=\"415\" cy=\"205\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#20262c\"/><text x=\"405\" y=\"189\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-size=\"22\" font-style=\"italic\">B</text>\n      <text x=\"478\" y=\"211\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-size=\"22\" font-style=\"italic\">x</text>\n      <text x=\"76\" y=\"20\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-size=\"22\" font-style=\"italic\">y</text>\n      <text x=\"65\" y=\"225\" font-family=\"Georgia\" font-size=\"18\">O</text>\n    </svg>\n  </div>","prompt":"Points <i>A</i> and <i>B</i> are shown in the <i>xy</i>-plane above. Point <i>C</i> (not shown) is above the <i>x</i>-axis so that the area of triangle <i>ABC</i> is 10. Which of the following could be the coordinates of <i>C</i>?<br><br>Indicate <u>all</u> such coordinates.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(0, 4)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1, 3)"},{"key":"C","text":"(2, 5)"},{"key":"D","text":"(3, 4)"},{"key":"E","text":"(4, 5)"}],"answer":["A","D"],"id":"quant-3-10","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q10","explanation":"정답은 A. (0, 4), D. (3, 4)입니다."},{"type":"multi","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">SELECTED DATA FOR GREETING CARD SALES</p>\n    <div class=\"data-layout\">\n      <div>\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Annual Revenue from All Greeting Card Sales, 1990–1993</p>\n        <div class=\"bar-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Annual revenue was approximately 4.7 billion dollars in 1990, 5.1 in 1991, 5.5 in 1992, and 6.0 in 1993.\">\n          <div class=\"y-label\">Revenue (in billions of dollars)</div>\n          <div class=\"plot\">\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:78.3%\"></div><span>1990</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:85%\"></div><span>1991</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:91.7%\"></div><span>1992</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:100%\"></div><span>1993</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"x-label\">Year</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Number of Greeting Cards Sold<br>for Ten Occasions in 1993</p>\n        <table class=\"data-table\">\n          <thead><tr><th>Occasion</th><th>Number of Cards</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td>Christmas</td><td>2.4 billion</td></tr><tr><td>Valentine’s Day</td><td>900 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Easter</td><td>158 million</td></tr><tr><td>Mother’s Day</td><td>155 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Father’s Day</td><td>102 million</td></tr><tr><td>Graduation</td><td>81 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Thanksgiving</td><td>42 million</td></tr><tr><td>Halloween</td><td>32 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>St. Patrick’s Day</td><td>18 million</td></tr><tr><td>Jewish New Year</td><td>12 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><th>Total</th><th>3.9 billion</th></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <p class=\"data-note\"><strong>Note:</strong> 1 billion = 1,000,000,000</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>","prompt":"In 1993 the average (arithmetic mean) price per card for all greeting cards sold was $1.25. For which of the following occasions was the number of cards sold in 1993 less than the total number of cards sold that year for occasions other than the ten occasions shown?<br><br>Indicate <u>all</u> such occasions.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Christmas"},{"key":"B","text":"Valentine’s Day"},{"key":"C","text":"Easter"},{"key":"D","text":"Mother’s Day"},{"key":"E","text":"Father’s Day"},{"key":"F","text":"Graduation"},{"key":"G","text":"Thanksgiving"},{"key":"H","text":"Halloween"}],"answer":["C","D","E","F","G","H"],"id":"quant-1-15","source":"Quant Practice Set 1 · Q15","explanation":"정답은 C. Easter, D. Mother’s Day, E. Father’s Day, F. Graduation, G. Thanksgiving, H. Halloween입니다."},{"type":"numeric","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block compact-data\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">AVERAGE RATING OF PRODUCT <i>X</i><br>GIVEN BY THREE GROUPS OF PEOPLE</p>\n    <table class=\"data-table\" aria-label=\"Average rating of Product X by group\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Number of<br>People in Group</th><th>Average Rating</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody><tr><td><i>A</i></td><td>45</td><td>3.8</td></tr><tr><td><i>B</i></td><td>25</td><td>4.6</td></tr><tr><td><i>C</i></td><td>30</td><td>4.2</td></tr></tbody>\n    </table>\n  </div>","prompt":"Each of the people in three groups gave a rating of Product <i>X</i> on a scale from 1 through 5. For each of the groups, the table above shows the number of people in the group and the average (arithmetic mean) of their ratings. What is the average of the ratings of the product given by the 100 people in the three groups combined?<br><br>Give your answer to the <u>nearest 0.1</u>.","answer":["4.1"],"id":"quant-3-11","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q11","explanation":"정답은 4.1입니다."},{"type":"single","prompt":"Of the students in a school, 20 percent are in the science club and 30 percent are in the band. If 25 percent of the students in the school are in the band but are not in the science club, what percent of the students who are in the science club are not in the band?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5%"},{"key":"B","text":"20%"},{"key":"C","text":"25%"},{"key":"D","text":"60%"},{"key":"E","text":"75%"}],"answer":["E"],"id":"quant-3-7","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q7","explanation":"정답은 E. 75%입니다."},{"type":"single","prompt":"The perimeter of a flat rectangular lawn is 42 meters. The width of the lawn is 75 percent of its length. What is the area of the lawn, in square meters?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"40.5"},{"key":"B","text":"96"},{"key":"C","text":"108"},{"key":"D","text":"192"},{"key":"E","text":"432"}],"answer":["C"],"id":"quant-4-11","source":"Quant Practice Set 4 · Q11","explanation":"정답은 C. 108입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"<i>S</i> = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8}","quantityA":"The number of 4-member subsets of <i>S</i>","quantityB":"The number of 5-member subsets of <i>S</i>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["A"],"id":"quant-5-6","source":"Quant Practice Set 5 · Q6","explanation":"정답은 A. Quantity A is greater.입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"<i>x</i>, <i>y</i>, and <i>z</i> are the lengths of the sides of a triangle.","quantityA":"<i>x</i> + <i>y</i> + <i>z</i>","quantityB":"2<i>z</i>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["A"],"id":"quant-1-5","source":"Quant Practice Set 1 · Q5","explanation":"정답은 A. Quantity A is greater.입니다."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">SELECTED DATA FOR GREETING CARD SALES</p>\n    <div class=\"data-layout\">\n      <div>\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Annual Revenue from All Greeting Card Sales, 1990–1993</p>\n        <div class=\"bar-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Annual revenue was approximately 4.7 billion dollars in 1990, 5.1 in 1991, 5.5 in 1992, and 6.0 in 1993.\">\n          <div class=\"y-label\">Revenue (in billions of dollars)</div>\n          <div class=\"plot\">\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:78.3%\"></div><span>1990</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:85%\"></div><span>1991</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:91.7%\"></div><span>1992</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:100%\"></div><span>1993</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"x-label\">Year</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Number of Greeting Cards Sold<br>for Ten Occasions in 1993</p>\n        <table class=\"data-table\">\n          <thead><tr><th>Occasion</th><th>Number of Cards</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td>Christmas</td><td>2.4 billion</td></tr><tr><td>Valentine’s Day</td><td>900 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Easter</td><td>158 million</td></tr><tr><td>Mother’s Day</td><td>155 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Father’s Day</td><td>102 million</td></tr><tr><td>Graduation</td><td>81 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Thanksgiving</td><td>42 million</td></tr><tr><td>Halloween</td><td>32 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>St. Patrick’s Day</td><td>18 million</td></tr><tr><td>Jewish New Year</td><td>12 million</td></tr>\n            <tr><th>Total</th><th>3.9 billion</th></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n        <p class=\"data-note\"><strong>Note:</strong> 1 billion = 1,000,000,000</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>","prompt":"Approximately what was the percent increase in the annual revenue from all greeting card sales from 1990 to 1993?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"50%"},{"key":"B","text":"45%"},{"key":"C","text":"39%"},{"key":"D","text":"28%"},{"key":"E","text":"20%"}],"answer":["D"],"id":"quant-1-14","source":"Quant Practice Set 1 · Q14","explanation":"정답은 D. 28%입니다."},{"type":"single","prompt":"A car dealer received a shipment of cars, half of which were black, with the remainder consisting of equal numbers of blue, silver, and white cars. During the next month, 70 percent of the black cars, 80 percent of the blue cars, 30 percent of the silver cars, and 40 percent of the white cars were sold. What percent of the cars in the shipment were sold during that month?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"36%"},{"key":"B","text":"50%"},{"key":"C","text":"55%"},{"key":"D","text":"60%"},{"key":"E","text":"72%"}],"answer":["D"],"id":"quant-4-9","source":"Quant Practice Set 4 · Q9","explanation":"정답은 D. 60%입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"","quantityA":"[(1/4)<sup>−1</sup> + (1/4)<sup>−2</sup> + (1/4)<sup>−3</sup>] / 4","quantityB":"21","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"quant-2-5","source":"Quant Practice Set 2 · Q5","explanation":"정답은 C. The two quantities are equal.입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"<i>x</i> is an integer, and 23 &lt; <i>x</i> &lt; 27.","quantityA":"The median of the five integers 23, 24, 26, 27, and <i>x</i>","quantityB":"25","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["D"],"id":"quant-3-2","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q2","explanation":"정답은 D. The relationship cannot be determined from the information given.입니다."}]},{"name":"Quantitative Reasoning · Section 2","minutes":26,"questions":[{"type":"numeric","prompt":"In a single line of people waiting to purchase tickets for a movie, there are currently 10 people behind Shandra. If 3 of the people who are currently in line ahead of Shandra purchase tickets and leave the line, and no one else leaves the line, there will be 8 people ahead of Shandra in line. How many people are in the line currently?","suffix":"people","answer":["22"],"id":"quant-1-11","source":"Quant Practice Set 1 · Q11","explanation":"정답은 22입니다."},{"type":"numeric","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block bird-data\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">SIGHTINGS OF SELECTED BIRD SPECIES<br>IN PARK <i>H</i> IN 1999, BY SEASON</p>\n    <div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"data-table\" aria-label=\"Bird sightings in Park H by season\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Species</th><th>Winter</th><th>Spring</th><th>Summer</th><th>Fall</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Cardinal</td><td>30</td><td>18</td><td>11</td><td>20</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Goldfinch</td><td>6</td><td>12</td><td>6</td><td>9</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Junco</td><td>12</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>6</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Nuthatch</td><td>8</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>4</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Robin</td><td>6</td><td>12</td><td>28</td><td>18</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Sparrow</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>23</td><td>22</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Wren</td><td>0</td><td>18</td><td>30</td><td>12</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table></div>\n  </div>","prompt":"By what percent did the number of wren sightings increase from spring to summer?<br><br>Give your answer to the <u>nearest whole percent</u>.","suffix":"%","answer":["67"],"id":"quant-3-15","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q15","explanation":"정답은 67입니다."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">INTERNET USE IN YEAR <i>X</i></p>\n    <div class=\"internet-visuals\">\n      <div class=\"pie-panel\">\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Distribution of Internet Users<br>Worldwide, by Region</p>\n        <div class=\"pie-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"United States 51 percent, Europe 29 percent, Japan 5 percent, and rest of world 15 percent.\">\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-us\">United States<br>51%</span>\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-europe\">Europe<br>29%</span>\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-japan\">Japan<br>5%</span>\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-rest\">Rest of World<br>15%</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"europe-panel\">\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Number of Internet Users in Europe<br>Total: 27.3 million</p>\n        <div class=\"internet-bars\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar graph of Internet users in seven European regions. Germany has approximately 6.5 million, France 5.9 million, Britain 5.0 million, Italy 1.5 million, Spain 1.0 million, Eastern Europe 1.8 million, and the rest of Europe 5.6 million.\">\n          <div class=\"y-label\">Number of Internet Users (in millions)</div>\n          <div class=\"plot\">\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:92.9%\"></div><span>Germany</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:84.3%\"></div><span>France</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:71.4%\"></div><span>Britain</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:21.4%\"></div><span>Italy</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:14.3%\"></div><span>Spain</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:25.7%\"></div><span>Eastern Europe</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:80%\"></div><span>Rest of Europe</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"x-label\">European Regions</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>","prompt":"Approximately what was the range of the numbers of Internet users in the seven regions of Europe shown in the bar graph?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"6.5 million"},{"key":"B","text":"5.5 million"},{"key":"C","text":"3.5 million"},{"key":"D","text":"3.0 million"},{"key":"E","text":"2.5 million"}],"answer":["B"],"id":"quant-2-13","source":"Quant Practice Set 2 · Q13","explanation":"정답은 B. 5.5 million입니다."},{"type":"multi","prompt":"In a factory, machine <i>A</i> operates on a cycle of 20 hours of work followed by 4 hours of rest, and machine <i>B</i> operates on a cycle of 40 hours of work followed by 8 hours of rest. Last week, the two machines began their respective cycles at 12 noon on Monday and continued until 12 noon on the following Saturday. On which days during that time period was there a time when both machines were at rest?<br><br>Indicate <u>all</u> such days.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Monday"},{"key":"B","text":"Tuesday"},{"key":"C","text":"Wednesday"},{"key":"D","text":"Thursday"},{"key":"E","text":"Friday"},{"key":"F","text":"Saturday"}],"answer":["C","E"],"id":"quant-5-13","source":"Quant Practice Set 5 · Q13","explanation":"정답은 C. Wednesday, E. Friday입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"<i>n</i> is a positive integer that is greater than 3 and has <i>d</i> positive divisors.","quantityA":"<i>n</i>","quantityB":"2<sup><i>d</i> − 1</sup>","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["D"],"id":"quant-4-2","source":"Quant Practice Set 4 · Q2","explanation":"정답은 D. The relationship cannot be determined from the information given.입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"The length of each side of rectangle <i>R</i> is an integer, and the area of <i>R</i> is 36.","quantityA":"The number of possible values of the perimeter of <i>R</i>","quantityB":"6","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["B"],"id":"quant-1-3","source":"Quant Practice Set 1 · Q3","explanation":"정답은 B. Quantity B is greater.입니다."},{"type":"single","prompt":"Which of the following functions <i>f</i> defined for all numbers <i>x</i> has the property that <i>f</i>(−<i>x</i>) = −<i>f</i>(<i>x</i>) for all numbers <i>x</i>?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"<i>f</i>(<i>x</i>) = <i>x</i><sup>3</sup> / (<i>x</i><sup>2</sup> + 1)"},{"key":"B","text":"<i>f</i>(<i>x</i>) = (<i>x</i><sup>2</sup> − 1) / (<i>x</i><sup>2</sup> + 1)"},{"key":"C","text":"<i>f</i>(<i>x</i>) = <i>x</i><sup>2</sup>(<i>x</i><sup>2</sup> − 1)"},{"key":"D","text":"<i>f</i>(<i>x</i>) = <i>x</i>(<i>x</i><sup>3</sup> − 1)"},{"key":"E","text":"<i>f</i>(<i>x</i>) = <i>x</i><sup>2</sup>(<i>x</i><sup>3</sup> − 1)"}],"answer":["A"],"id":"quant-1-9","source":"Quant Practice Set 1 · Q9","explanation":"정답은 A. f ( x ) = x 3 / ( x 2 + 1)입니다."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">INTERNET USE IN YEAR <i>X</i></p>\n    <div class=\"internet-visuals\">\n      <div class=\"pie-panel\">\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Distribution of Internet Users<br>Worldwide, by Region</p>\n        <div class=\"pie-chart\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"United States 51 percent, Europe 29 percent, Japan 5 percent, and rest of world 15 percent.\">\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-us\">United States<br>51%</span>\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-europe\">Europe<br>29%</span>\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-japan\">Japan<br>5%</span>\n          <span class=\"pie-label pie-rest\">Rest of World<br>15%</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"europe-panel\">\n        <p class=\"data-title\">Number of Internet Users in Europe<br>Total: 27.3 million</p>\n        <div class=\"internet-bars\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar graph of Internet users in seven European regions. Germany has approximately 6.5 million, France 5.9 million, Britain 5.0 million, Italy 1.5 million, Spain 1.0 million, Eastern Europe 1.8 million, and the rest of Europe 5.6 million.\">\n          <div class=\"y-label\">Number of Internet Users (in millions)</div>\n          <div class=\"plot\">\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:92.9%\"></div><span>Germany</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:84.3%\"></div><span>France</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:71.4%\"></div><span>Britain</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:21.4%\"></div><span>Italy</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:14.3%\"></div><span>Spain</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:25.7%\"></div><span>Eastern Europe</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bar-wrap\"><div class=\"bar\" style=\"height:80%\"></div><span>Rest of Europe</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"x-label\">European Regions</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>","prompt":"The number of Internet users in the United States was approximately how many times the number of Internet users in Italy?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5"},{"key":"B","text":"15"},{"key":"C","text":"20"},{"key":"D","text":"25"},{"key":"E","text":"35"}],"answer":["E"],"id":"quant-2-14","source":"Quant Practice Set 2 · Q14","explanation":"정답은 E. 35입니다."},{"type":"single","prompt":"The relationship between temperature <i>C</i>, in degrees Celsius, and temperature <i>F</i>, in degrees Fahrenheit, is given by the formula <i>F</i> = (9/5)<i>C</i> + 32. If a recipe calls for an oven temperature of 210 degrees Celsius, what is the oven temperature in degrees Fahrenheit?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"320"},{"key":"B","text":"350"},{"key":"C","text":"410"},{"key":"D","text":"420"},{"key":"E","text":"500"}],"answer":["C"],"id":"quant-3-6","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q6","explanation":"정답은 C. 410입니다."},{"type":"single","prompt":"Each year, the members of a book club select novels and nonfiction books to read. The club meets 3 times to discuss each novel and 5 times to discuss each nonfiction book they select. Last year, the club met 52 times and discussed 12 books. How many novels did the club discuss last year?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"2"},{"key":"B","text":"4"},{"key":"C","text":"5"},{"key":"D","text":"7"},{"key":"E","text":"14"}],"answer":["B"],"id":"quant-3-8","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q8","explanation":"정답은 B. 4입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"At a club meeting, there are 10 more club members than nonmembers. The number of club members at the meeting is <i>c</i>.","quantityA":"The total number of people at the club meeting","quantityB":"2<i>c</i> − 10","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"quant-4-1","source":"Quant Practice Set 4 · Q1","explanation":"정답은 C. The two quantities are equal.입니다."},{"type":"qc","context":"The function <i>f</i> is defined by <i>f</i>((<i>x</i> + 3)/2) = 3<i>x</i><sup>2</sup> − <i>x</i> + 5 for all numbers <i>x</i>.","quantityA":"<i>f</i>(4)","quantityB":"75","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Quantity A is greater."},{"key":"B","text":"Quantity B is greater."},{"key":"C","text":"The two quantities are equal."},{"key":"D","text":"The relationship cannot be determined from the information given."}],"answer":["C"],"id":"quant-3-4","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q4","explanation":"정답은 C. The two quantities are equal.입니다."},{"type":"numeric","prompt":"From 2011 to 2012, Jack’s annual salary increased by 10 percent and Arnie’s annual salary decreased by 5 percent. If their annual salaries were equal in 2012, then Arnie’s annual salary in 2011 was what percent greater than Jack’s annual salary in 2011?<br><br>Give your answer to the <u>nearest 0.1 percent</u>.","suffix":"%","answer":["15.8"],"id":"quant-5-15","source":"Quant Practice Set 5 · Q15","explanation":"정답은 15.8입니다."},{"type":"single","stimulus":"\n  <div class=\"data-block bird-data\">\n    <p class=\"data-title\">SIGHTINGS OF SELECTED BIRD SPECIES<br>IN PARK <i>H</i> IN 1999, BY SEASON</p>\n    <div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"data-table\" aria-label=\"Bird sightings in Park H by season\">\n      <thead><tr><th>Species</th><th>Winter</th><th>Spring</th><th>Summer</th><th>Fall</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Cardinal</td><td>30</td><td>18</td><td>11</td><td>20</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Goldfinch</td><td>6</td><td>12</td><td>6</td><td>9</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Junco</td><td>12</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>6</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Nuthatch</td><td>8</td><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>4</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Robin</td><td>6</td><td>12</td><td>28</td><td>18</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Sparrow</td><td>20</td><td>19</td><td>23</td><td>22</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Wren</td><td>0</td><td>18</td><td>30</td><td>12</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table></div>\n  </div>","prompt":"Which of the following is closest to the average (arithmetic mean) number of cardinal sightings for the 4 seasons?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"12"},{"key":"B","text":"14"},{"key":"C","text":"16"},{"key":"D","text":"18"},{"key":"E","text":"20"}],"answer":["E"],"id":"quant-3-14","source":"Quant Practice Set 3 · Q14","explanation":"정답은 E. 20입니다."},{"type":"multi","prompt":"Two different positive integers <i>x</i> and <i>y</i> are selected from the odd integers that are less than 10. If <i>z</i> = <i>x</i> + <i>y</i> and <i>z</i> is less than 10, which of the following integers could be the sum of <i>x</i>, <i>y</i>, and <i>z</i>?<br><br>Indicate <u>all</u> such integers.","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"8"},{"key":"B","text":"9"},{"key":"C","text":"10"},{"key":"D","text":"12"},{"key":"E","text":"14"},{"key":"F","text":"15"},{"key":"G","text":"16"},{"key":"H","text":"18"}],"answer":["A","D","G"],"id":"quant-2-10","source":"Quant Practice Set 2 · Q10","explanation":"정답은 A. 8, D. 12, G. 16입니다."}]}]};
